---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

// Every statement here must match what the code does. When the code changes -
// a new table, a new processor, a new retention period - this page changes in
// the same pull request. An inaccurate privacy policy is worse than none.
const updated = "25 September 2026";

const collected = [
  {
    what: "Account",
    items: "Email address, a password hash (Argon2; we never see or store the password), whether the address is verified, your role, whether two-factor is on, and the public keys of any passkeys you add (with the name you give each one). A passkey's private key never leaves your device or password manager.",
    why: "To sign you in and keep the account yours.",
  },
  {
    what: "Profile",
    items: "Handle, display name, bio, avatar colour, timezone, units, week start, planned training days, and your birth year (the year only, not a date of birth).",
    why: "To run the app for you. The birth year exists only for the age rules below.",
  },
  {
    what: "Training",
    items: "Sessions (discipline, time, duration, distance, elevation, per-kilometre splits from imported tracks, effort, how it felt, private notes and private tags), sets and supersets, routines, training plans (including any a coach suggested), custom exercises, gear you track (shoes, bikes) and which sessions used it, gyms you add (with their equipment and plates) and which sessions were there, notes you pin to exercises, streak wagers, streak targets and requirements, monthly goals, rest days you log, repairs, pauses (with an optional private note), and anything you import from a file.",
    why: "This is the product. Streaks, records, XP and badges are computed from it.",
  },
  {
    what: "Body metrics",
    items: "Weigh-ins (weight, time and when in your day), measurements and a weight goal, only if you choose to record them. Progress photos are stored only on your own device and are never sent to us.",
    why: "For your own trend. Never shared, never ranked, never in any feed, never rewarded.",
  },
  {
    what: "Social",
    items: "Who you follow and who follows you, blocks, kudos, comments, groups and their announcements, challenges, streak buddies, encouragement you send, and reports you make.",
    why: "Only if you use these features. People under 16 cannot.",
  },
  {
    what: "Notifications",
    items: "Your in-app inbox, your per-category choices, and, if you enable push, the browser's push subscription endpoint and keys.",
    why: "To tell you what you asked to be told.",
  },
  {
    what: "Security",
    items: "Active sessions, and a history of sign-ins, password, email, passkey and two-factor changes, exports, calendar-link changes and which version of the terms you accepted, each with the IP address and browser user agent. Failed sign-in attempts are recorded with the IP address and a keyed hash of the address tried (never the address itself), and linked to your account only if the address is yours.",
    why: "So you can spot activity that wasn't you, and so we can investigate abuse.",
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — PaceStreak"
  description="What PaceStreak collects, why, who can see it, how long it is kept, and how to export or delete all of it. No analytics, no advertising, no selling data."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <section class="py-16 sm:py-20">
    <div class="wrap max-w-2xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[0.92rem] text-dim">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <div class="prose-page mt-10">
        <p>
          The short version: we collect what it takes to run a training log,
          nothing to profile you, and you can take all of it with you or delete
          it at any time. There is no analytics, no advertising and no selling
          of data, and the sites and app load nothing from third parties.
        </p>
        <p>
          PaceStreak is not open to the public yet. The website sections apply
          now; the account sections apply from the moment accounts open.
          Questions go to{" "}
          <a href="mailto:hello@pacestreak.com">hello@pacestreak.com</a>, read
          by a person.
        </p>

        <h2>The websites</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>www.pacestreak.com</strong> and{" "}
          <strong>blog.pacestreak.com</strong> set no cookies, store nothing in
          your browser, and run no analytics or tracking. A content security
          policy of <code>default-src 'self'</code> makes the browser refuse
          any third-party script, so this is enforced, not just intended.
          Cloudflare, which serves the sites, processes the IP address and
          request needed to deliver each page and keeps operational logs; we
          receive no per-visitor reports.
        </p>

        <h2>What the app collects, and why</h2>
      </div>

      <dl class="mt-6 divide-y divide-line rounded-[--radius-xl2] border border-line bg-surface">
        {
          collected.map((c) => (
            <div class="px-5 py-4 sm:px-6">
              <dt class="font-semibold">{c.what}</dt>
              <dd class="mt-1.5 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">{c.items}</dd>
              <dd class="mt-1.5 text-[0.9rem] text-dim">{c.why}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>

      <div class="prose-page mt-10">
        <h2>Crash reports</h2>
        <p>
          If the app crashes, it sends us the error message, the stack trace,
          the page's path and your browser's user agent so we can fix it.
          Nothing else: no account, no query string (which can carry a
          one-time link), no content from the page. Crash reports are kept
          for 30 days.
        </p>

        <h2>What we don't collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>No location, GPS or map data. Files you import are read for time, distance and elevation; routes are not stored.</li>
          <li>No contacts, photos, or data from other apps or devices, except files you upload.</li>
          <li>No advertising identifiers, fingerprinting or analytics of any kind.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Who can see what</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Nothing is public by default.</strong> Your activity reaches
            only followers you have approved. You can make your profile private
            or public, or pause sharing entirely.
          </li>
          <li>
            Visibility is checked every time something is read, so going
            private, pausing or blocking someone also hides what they could see
            before.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Groups</strong> see your handle, streak and this week's
            progress, and whether your week counted toward the group's
            streak. A coach sees your sessions, and your running plan's
            progress, only if you turn that on for their group, and loses
            access the moment you turn it off. A coach can suggest a plan to
            you; it only starts if you start it.
          </li>
          <li>
            A <strong>streak buddy</strong>, once you both accept, sees your
            days trained this week against your target and whether you are
            paused. Never your sessions, notes or the reason for a pause.
            Either of you can end it at any time, and blocking ends it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Never shown to anyone else:</strong> your email, notes,
            tags, gear, gyms, pinned exercise notes, splits, training plans,
            monthly goals, rest days, body metrics and weight goal, pause reasons, passkeys, security history, calendar link
            and imports.
          </li>
          <li>
            Leaderboards include you only if you opt in, and never rank
            anything about your body.
          </li>
          <li>
            PaceStreak staff can access account data to operate the service,
            respond to reports and investigate abuse. Every moderation action
            is recorded in an audit log that cannot be edited.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Age</h2>
        <p>
          You must be <strong>13 or older</strong> to have an account. Under
          16, an account is <strong>private only</strong>: no feed, no groups,
          no leaderboards and no public profile, whatever the settings say. We
          ask for a birth year to apply these rules, and nothing else about
          your age.
        </p>

        <h2>Service providers</h2>
        <p>
          We use as few as possible and never share data for anyone else's
          purposes. Today that is Cloudflare, which hosts the websites and the
          app, and Zoho, which receives mail sent to hello@pacestreak.com. The
          provider hosting the API and database, and the provider that sends
          account email, will be named here before accounts open. Web push
          messages pass through your browser's own push service (for example
          Google's or Apple's), encrypted so that service cannot read them.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Your data is kept while your account exists.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Deleting your account</strong> schedules it for 30 days
            later and signs you out everywhere. Sign in during those 30 days to
            cancel. After that, the account and everything linked to it is
            permanently deleted.
          </li>
          <li>
            Database backups, readable only by the server operator, are kept for up to 14 days, so deleted
            data can survive in a backup for up to 14 days after deletion
            before it expires.
          </li>
          <li>Failed sign-in records and crash reports are kept for 30 days.</li>
          <li>Operational server logs are kept for a short period and then rotated away.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Your controls and rights</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Export everything</strong> at any time from Settings → Data:
            a complete JSON archive, CSV files, or a calendar file.
          </li>
          <li><strong>Correct</strong> anything from the app, or ask us.</li>
          <li><strong>Delete</strong> your account from Settings → Data.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Object or restrict:</strong> turn off social features,
            gamification, reminders, push and email by category, and revoke
            the calendar link, a coach's access or a buddy at any time. The
            monthly backup reminder is off unless you turn it on, and it
            links into the app rather than carrying any of your data.
          </li>
          <li>
            For anything else, including a question about how your data is
            handled, write to{" "}
            <a href="mailto:hello@pacestreak.com">hello@pacestreak.com</a>. We
            answer within 30 days. You can also complain to your local data
            protection authority.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
          Passwords must be at least 16 characters and are hashed with Argon2.
          Sessions use short-lived tokens that are never written to browser
          storage, with theft detection on refresh. Passkeys and two-factor
          authentication are available; for a passkey only the public key is
          stored, and two-factor secrets are encrypted at rest. The calendar
          link is stored only as a hash. The details are on the{" "}
          <a href="/security">security page</a>. If we ever discover a breach
          affecting your data, we will tell you and the relevant authority as
          the law requires.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          This page is versioned in{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/PaceStreak">our repositories</a>, so
          every change has a date and a record. If a change affects how your
          data is used, we will tell account holders in the app before it
          takes effect.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
